{
  "$comment": [
    "Corpus for `appearance_sanitize_gate_tier3_equivalence` — v4",
    "`lib/image-gen/appearance-resolution.ts` `sanitizeAppearancesIfNeeded`, the",
    "five-rule gate. Until [cc65d6bfc / bug 133] NO harness family and no oracle",
    "case drove that function directly: the story and image-generation tier-3",
    "families reach it only incidentally, and the image one keeps the Concierge OFF",
    "throughout. This family drives it head-on.",
    "",
    "The grid (v4 `3b463d6b1`, #76 — the Concierge POLICY replaced the retired",
    "mode) is the policy {off duty, Moderated with the pre-screen on, Unmoderated}",
    "x isDangerousChat {t,f} x routesDangerousToUncensored {t,f} x classification",
    "{safe, dangerous} = 24 rows, each row's policy resolved from its stored",
    "`concierge` settings WITH its `chat`; plus a customClassificationPrompt row,",
    "two sanitizer-answer edges, and #76's three pass-through policies (Moderated",
    "without the pre-screen, Locked, an exempt help chat). Some combinations no",
    "real caller produces: the fourth parameter is an argument, not a derivation,",
    "and the function's contract covers them.",
    "them.",
    "",
    "Each case carries its own TOKEN inside the appearance text. That is not",
    "decoration: the classification cache is keyed by a sha256 of the content and is",
    "process-global on BOTH sides, so two rows sharing appearance text would make the",
    "second one's completion-call comparand measure the cache instead of the gate.",
    "",
    "Comparands per row: the returned appearances (physicalDescription /",
    "clothingDescription / wasSanitized) AND the number of completion calls with",
    "their recorded keys — which is what proves WHICH rule fired. Rule 1 and rule 2",
    "make zero calls, rule 3-safe makes one, rule 4 makes one, rule 5 makes two.",
    "",
    "NOT compared: `llm_logs`. v4's classify path logs a DANGER_CLASSIFICATION row,",
    "but jest.setup no-ops the logging service and un-mocking it would need this",
    "family to provision a whole instance for a projection two other families",
    "(danger_gatekeeper_tier3, story_background_job_tier3) already diff. Recorded",
    "here so the omission is a decision and not an oversight.",
    "",
    "[97b25fc53] P4.D239 — the drape. Rows AGCASE31..40 pose the sanitize MODE",
    "(`mode`, the 8th argument; absent = v4's `redress` default) and the conceal",
    "reply's `undressed` flag (`undressed`, spliced per character into the answer",
    "whatever the mode). They pin: the three-way merge (changed + undressed; an",
    "unchanged ECHO + undressed keeps its clothing with `wasSanitized` false; changed",
    "+ not undressed); v4's STRICT `=== true` (`\"true\"` and `1` read false); the",
    "junk fallback carrying no `undressed` in conceal; redress dropping a stray",
    "`true`; rule 4 skipping the sanitize call in conceal too; a text ending in `.`",
    "(the story builder's `..` is pinned in the story family — here the text rides",
    "through unchanged); and `sanitizeThrows` — v4's `Sanitization failed` WARN arm",
    "in BOTH modes (the N3 gap the Rust header recorded). Comparands gained:",
    "`needsConcealment` (present only when true), `concealPromptCalls` (the mock's",
    "second probe — which prompt the mode picked), and `logLines` (v4's REAL logger",
    "calls for the gate + the sanitizer's pre-call DEBUG, keys in v4's order)."
  ],
